{
  "id": "Compound::DB01435 - Gene::1565",
  "verbalization": "Antipyrine is shown to bind to Cyp2c19, a cytochrome P450 enzyme, which is involved in the metabolism of xenobiotics and eicosanoid synthesis. This binding leads to the participation of Cyp2c19 in multiple metabolic pathways, including the epoxygenation and monooxygenation of arachidonic acid. These pathways are ultimately linked to Cyp2d6, suggesting a potential mechanism by which Antipyrine may influence Cyp2d6 activity. The evidence from the three paths indicates that Antipyrine's interaction with Cyp2c19 is central to its effect on Cyp2d6, as Cyp2c19 serves as a bridge between Antipyrine and Cyp2d6 through distinct but related metabolic functions. The consistent binding and participation relationships across the paths support a mechanistic link, though the exact nature of the interaction between Antipyrine and Cyp2d6 remains to be fully elucidated.",
